</attention3>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1426053001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove engine assembly from vehicle. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1426025"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove flywheel. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1426030"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove pistons and connecting rods. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1426047"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove oil seal housing (1).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140132.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "60.360mm" ver = "02" gw = "148" gh = "155"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove rear oil seal from oil seal housing.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove CKP sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1326023"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove main bearing cap bolts in numerical order (“1 – “10”) evenly and gradually.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove main bearing caps.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140236.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "61.063mm" ver = "01" gw = "191" gh = "157"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove crankshaft from cylinder block.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove sensor plate from crankshaft, if necessary.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Use T-30 security Torx<sup>&#174;</sup> to loosen sensor plate screws.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove piston cooling jets (1), if necessary.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140237.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "53.582mm" ver = "01" gw = "165" gh = "135"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove oil cooler, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove ISG, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1A26005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove water pump, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1626015"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove PCV valve, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1226008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove breather plate (1), if necessary.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140238.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "51.971mm" ver = "01" gw = "200" gh = "131"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove knock sensor, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1326026"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove piston cooling jet valve, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526014"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1426053002">
<title>
Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1426054">Crankshaft Inspection:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1426055">Main Bearing Inspection:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1426056">Sensor Plate Inspection:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1426031">Flywheel Inspection:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1426058">Cylinder Block Inspection:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
The engine will seize up if it is operated when the parts listed below are not properly lubricated.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Lubricate all the friction surfaces of these parts with engine oil before installing them.
</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Crankshaft journals
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Main bearings (Sliding surface)
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Thrust bearings
</ptxt>
</item>
</list2>
<item>
<ptxt>
Using main bearing cap bolts that are deformed exceeding the service limit could lead to engine problems.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
When main bearing cap bolts are reused, check that main bearing cap bolts are not deformed exceeding the service limit referring to “Main Bearing Cap Bolt” under 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1426055">Main Bearing Inspection:K14D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install new piston cooling jet valve, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526014"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install knock sensor, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1326026"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install breather plate (1) as follows, if removed.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Fit new gasket (2) to breather plate.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140239.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "46.775mm" ver = "01" gw = "127" gh = "116"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Install breather plate (1) to cylinder block, and then tighten breather plate bolts No.1 in numerical order (“1” – “6”) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D269">
<t-part>
Breather plate bolt No.1
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
11
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
1.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
8.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Install new breather plate bolt No.2 (2) and tighten it to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D270">
<t-part>
Breather plate bolt No.2
</t-part>
<t-part1>
b
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
11
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
1.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
8.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140240.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "54.558mm" ver = "01" gw = "200" gh = "138"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install PCV valve, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1226008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install water pump, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1626015"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install ISG, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1A26005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install oil cooler, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1526005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install piston cooling jets (1), if removed, and then tighten piston cooling jet bolts (2).
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D271">
<t-part>
Piston cooling jet bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
11
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
1.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
8.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140241.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "53.582mm" ver = "01" gw = "165" gh = "135"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install sensor plate (1) as follows, if removed.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Put sensor plate to crankshaft (2) as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Fix position of sensor plate inserting a spring pin (3) (09205-05006) to crankshaft hole (4) through oblong hole (5) in sensor plate.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Tighten sensor plate screws to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D272">
<t-part>
Sensor plate screw
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
11
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
1.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
8.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A142112.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "48.584mm" ver = "01" gw = "209" gh = "121"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Remove the spring pin.
</ptxt>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that dowel pins are installed to cylinder block securely.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install main bearings to cylinder block and main bearing caps as follows.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
If oil is present between the bearing backside and cylinder block or main bearing cap surface, the bearing could heat up to very high temperature, resulting in seizure.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Thoroughly wipe off any trace of oil that is present between the bearing backside and cylinder block or main bearing cap surface.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Install main bearing halves (1) with oil groove (2) to cylinder block.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140242.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "54.387mm" ver = "01" gw = "223" gh = "138"/>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Install other main bearing halves without oil groove to main bearing caps.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Check mating surfaces (5) of bearing backside and corresponding cylinder block and main bearing cap are clean and dry.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Fit the tab (1) on each bearing into groove (2) in cylinder block and main bearing cap.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Press bearing end (3) until it fully seats in cylinder block and main bearing cap.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Apply engine oil to sliding surface (4) of main bearing halves at cylinder block side.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I8T401142036.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "38.847mm" ver = "01" gw = "130" gh = "94"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply engine oil to thrust bearings (1) and install them to cylinder block between No.2 and No.3 cylinders with oil grooves (2) facing outward.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140140.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "50.951mm" ver = "01" gw = "174" gh = "128"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check cleanliness of crankshaft journal and place crankshaft on cylinder block and then apply engine oil to crankshaft journal.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install main bearing caps according to the following procedure.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Using main bearing cap bolts that are deformed exceeding the service limit could lead to engine problems.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Before installing main bearing cap, check that main bearing cap bolts are not deformed exceeding the service limit referring to “Main Bearing Cap Bolt” under 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1426055">Main Bearing Inspection:K14D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
For accurate angle tightening of the bolt, use commercially available tightening angle gauge.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IJHA0A140061.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "53.411mm" ver = "01" gw = "151" gh = "135"/>
</figure>
</attention3>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Check dowel pins are fitted to main bearing caps.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Point arrow mark on cap to crankshaft pulley side and set main bearing caps to cylinder block.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Apply engine oil to bolt thread and seat of main bearing cap bolts.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Tighten main bearing cap bolts to 20 N&#183;m (2.0 kgf-m, 15.0 lbf-ft) in numerical order (“1” – “10”) as shown using a 12-point socket wrenches.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
In the same manner as in Step d), tighten them to 40 N&#183;m (4.1 kgf-m, 29.5 lbf-ft).
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Retighten all main bearing cap bolts 60&#176; in numerical order as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D273">
<t-part>
Main bearing cap bolt*
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-note>
20 N&#183;m &#8594; 40 N&#183;m &#8594; +60&#176; (2.0 kgf-m &#8594; 4.1 kgf-m &#8594; +60&#176;, 15.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 29.5 lbf-ft &#8594; +60&#176;)
</t-note>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140243.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "61.063mm" ver = "01" gw = "218" gh = "157"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that crankshaft rotates smoothly when turning it by hand.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install CKP sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1326023"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Clean sealing surface between oil seal housing and cylinder block.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install new rear oil seal (1) to oil seal housing (2) using special tool.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1D272">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09914-88410">
09914–88410
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<spec>
<title>
Rear oil seal installing position (depth)
</title>
<ptxt>
“a”: 1.0 mm (0.039 in.)
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I7V20A141110.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "54.503mm" ver = "01" gw = "218" gh = "138"/>
</figure>
</spec>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Check that dowel pins (2) are installed to oil seal housing (1) as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean mating surfaces of cylinder block and oil seal housing.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply sealant to mating surface of oil seal housing (1).
</ptxt>
<materials>
<materialitem name = "SUZUKI Bond No.1217G" id = "M1D209" uid = "-491504098">
<m-part>
“A”
</m-part>
<m-desc>
Sealant
</m-desc>
<m-number>
99000–31260
</m-number>
<m-name>
SUZUKI Bond No.1217G
</m-name>
</materialitem>
</materials>
<spec>
<title>
Sealant amount for oil seal housing
</title>
<ptxt>
Width: “a”: 3 mm (0.12 in.)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Height “b”: 2 mm (0.08 in.)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A142113.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "53.230mm" ver = "01" gw = "174" gh = "134"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install oil seal housing (1) according to the following procedure.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Apply engine oil to oil seal lip.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Within 2 minutes after applying sealant, install oil seal housing using special tool to cylinder block.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Turning over of oil seal lip or coming off of the inside spring will cause oil leakage.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
While installing oil seal housing, pay attention not to turn over oil seal lip nor disengage the inside spring.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Tighten new oil seal housing bolts (2) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1D273">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09911-98410">
09911–98410
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D274">
<t-part>
Oil seal housing bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
